  <div class="alert-info sec">
    <span>ℹ️</span>
    <span>By registering for the <strong>Iskcon Tirupati Essay Writing Contest 2026</strong>, you agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions. Please read them carefully before completing your registration.</span>
  </div>

  <div class="card sec">
    <div class="sec-title"><span>👥</span>Eligibility</div>
    <ul class="styled-list">
      <li>The contest is open to <strong>all residents of India</strong> across all age groups</li>
      <li>Two age categories are available: <strong>0 to 25 years</strong> and <strong>Above 25 years</strong></li>
      <li>Participants under 18 must have parental or guardian consent to register</li>
      <li>Registration requires a valid mobile number and email address</li>
      <li>Each participant may register for multiple contest categories</li>
      <li>Employees and immediate family members of ISKCON are eligible to participate</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card sec">
    <div class="sec-title"><span>💳</span>Registration &amp; Payment</div>
    <ul class="styled-list">
      <li>Registration fee of <strong>₹399 per contest category</strong> is required</li>
      <li>The Combo Pack (all 4 contests) is available at a special bundled price</li>
      <li>Payment must be completed through our secure payment gateway</li>
      <li>Registration is confirmed only after successful payment verification</li>
      <li>Participants will receive confirmation via registered mobile number/email</li>
      <li>Registration fees are non-transferable between contest categories</li>
      <li>Refunds are subject to our <a href="/refund-policy" style="color:#fbbf24;font-weight:700">Refund Policy</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card card-blue sec">
    <div class="sec-title"><span>✍️</span>Essay Submission Rules</div>
    <ul class="styled-list">
      <li>All essays must be <strong>original work</strong> created solely by the participant</li>
      <li>Essay length must be between <strong>500 and 2,000 words</strong></li>
      <li>Only <strong>PDF or DOCX</strong> file formats are accepted</li>
      <li>Maximum file size: <strong>5 MB</strong></li>
      <li>Each participant gets a maximum of <strong>3 upload attempts</strong> per contest (last upload counts)</li>
      <li>Essays must align with devotional and cultural themes of the respective sacred text</li>
      <li>Submissions must be made before the stated deadline: <strong>04 September 2026</strong></li>
      <li>Late submissions will not be accepted under any circumstances</li>
      <li><strong>Plagiarism</strong> or copying will result in immediate disqualification</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card sec">
    <div class="sec-title"><span>🏆</span>Prizes &amp; Awards</div>
    <ul class="styled-list">
      <li>Winners will be selected by a panel of qualified judges appointed by ISKCON Tirupati</li>
      <li>The organiser's decision on winners is <strong>final and binding</strong></li>
      <li>Prize amounts will be communicated directly to winners after announcement</li>
      <li>Prizes are non-transferable and cannot be exchanged for cash alternatives</li>
      <li>Winners must provide necessary documentation (ID proof, bank details) for prize distribution</li>
      <li>Tax implications on cash prizes are the sole responsibility of the winners</li>
      <li>All participants receive a <strong>Digital Certificate of Participation</strong></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card sec">
    <div class="sec-title"><span>📚</span>Gift Book Delivery</div>
    <ul class="styled-list">
      <li>Gift Books selected during checkout will be delivered to the address provided at registration</li>
      <li>Participants who select donation mode — books will be donated by the temple on their behalf</li>
      <li>Participants who select temple pickup — must collect from the contest stall at the temple</li>
      <li>Delivery timelines depend on courier availability and location</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card sec">
    <div class="sec-title"><span>©️</span>Intellectual Property</div>
    <p class="body-text">By submitting your essay, you grant ISKCON Tirupati a <strong>non-exclusive licence</strong> to use, display, and promote your submission for contest purposes and promotional activities. You <strong>retain full ownership rights</strong> to your original work. ISKCON will always credit participants when using their work publicly.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card card-red sec">
    <div class="sec-title"><span>⚠️</span>Disqualification</div>
    <p class="body-text">Participants may be disqualified without refund in the following cases:</p>
    <ul class="styled-list">
      <li>Submission of plagiarised, AI-generated, or copied content</li>
      <li>Violation of contest rules or guidelines</li>
      <li>Submission after the stated deadline</li>
      <li>Use of offensive, inappropriate, or irrelevant content</li>
      <li>Providing false registration information</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card sec">
    <div class="sec-title"><span>🔒</span>Limitation of Liability</div>
    <p class="body-text">ISKCON Tirupati and the contest organisers are not liable for any technical issues, lost submissions, or delays caused by circumstances beyond our control (force majeure, internet outages, etc.). We reserve the right to modify contest rules, deadlines, or prize values, or cancel the contest if necessary, with prior notice to registered participants.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card card-gold sec">
    <div class="sec-title"><span>📞</span>Questions About These Terms</div>
    <div class="info-row">
      <div class="info-icon">📧</div>
      <div><div class="info-label">Email</div><div class="info-val"><a href="mailto:support@iskconcontest.org">support@iskconcontest.org</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-row">
      <div class="info-icon">📱</div>
      <div><div class="info-label">Phone / WhatsApp</div><div class="info-val"><a href="tel:+919493805059">+91-9493805059</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-row">
      <div class="info-icon">📍</div>
      <div><div class="info-label">Address</div><div class="info-val">Hare Krishna Land, Hare Krishna Road, Vinayaka Nagar, Tirupati – 517501, Andhra Pradesh</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
